cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SenideOG"
abstract: >
  Builds a species x orthogroup matrix for ~500 Viridiplantae reference
  proteomes via OrthoFinder (core inference + assignment), replacing the
  GO-term unit used by prior comparative analyses with orthology inferred
  directly from sequences. "senide" is Basque for "relative/kin", + OG for
  orthogroup.
authors:
  - family-names: de Martín-Agirre
    given-names: Iñigo
    email: imartinagirre@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0374-6504"
version: "v0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-09-11"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/inigodemartin/SenideOG"
keywords:
  - orthology
  - orthogroups
  - comparative genomics
  - Viridiplantae
  - OrthoFinder
  - phylogenomics
